From f45a39cd1b309de2b69a7b66f4efc50cfc8a165e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:04:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: settle the bottom tab sheet with a spring from the
 finger's speed

The bottom-bar tab sheet settled with a fixed 320 ms animator that
dropped the release velocity, and the page dim and scale stopped at
half, so a fling to full felt forced.

Releasing a drag now settles with a damped spring (stiffness 700,
damping ratio 0.9) that starts from the finger's velocity. Tapping open,
Back and close() use the same spring from rest. A new drag cancels the
spring and continues 1:1 from the current progress. Shown progress is
clamped to [0, 1] and the close restore runs once when the spring rests
at 0.

Page dim and scale follow progress past half: half looks as before
(scale 0.95, scrim 0.35) and full goes further (scale 0.9375, scrim
0.4375). The top-bar sheet and the side drawer keep their animator.
